protesters attack a china mobile shop in  the past few days dozens of businesses  in Hong Kong have been vandalized during  clashes protesters often target  companies from the mainland such as the  state-owned telecom providers the big  Chinese banks and other industries tied  to the Beijing government but there are  less obvious choices like this famous US  coffee brand  Starbucks has been one of the top  targets this one has been vandalized  twice first they trashed the entrance  then then the next day the company set  up these wooden panels to protect it and  then the next day the protesters took  down these panels and continued trashing  this shop so it feels saddening and  frustrating at the same time this  consequence is due to the government's  which didn't listen to the citizens in  online groups protesters post messages  explaining their choice of targets Hong  Kong Starbucks branches are run by the  local caterer max Eames the company drew  the wrath of the protesters when the  founders daughter held a speech at the  UN Human Rights Council denouncing the  protests lexemes has distanced itself  from her statement saying she holds no  official position in the business but to  no avail  the logic of conflict has reached Hong  Kong's businesses between the ire of the  protesters and repercussions on the  Chinese market many of them are facing a  tough choice for this Starbucks branch  the only thing to do now is to renovate  and hope that they won't be targeted a  third time
 

